  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Write down the general form of a monic quadratic whose axis of symmetry is $x=-2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p34-q15-general",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=(x+2)^2+k$, where $k$ is any real number.",
          "worked": "In $y=a(x-h)^2+k$, the axis is $x=h$. Monic means $a=1$, and the given axis gives $h=-2$.\n\n$$y=(x+2)^2+k,\\qquad k\\in\\mathbb R.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p34-q15-conditions",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "Hence find the equation of such a quadratic which also:",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 3,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p34-q15-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "passes through $(0,0)$,",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y=(x+2)^2-4$",
              "worked": "Substitute $(0,0)$ into $y=(x+2)^2+k$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}0&=(0+2)^2+k\\\\0&=4+k\\\\k&=-4\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$y=(x+2)^2-4.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 44
          },
          {
            "id": "p34-q15-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "passes through $(5,1)$,",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y=(x+2)^2-48$",
              "worked": "Substitute $(5,1)$ into $y=(x+2)^2+k$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}1&=(5+2)^2+k\\\\1&=49+k\\\\k&=-48\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$y=(x+2)^2-48.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 44
          },
          {
            "id": "p34-q15-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "has a zero at $x=1$,",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y=(x+2)^2-9$",
              "worked": "The zero gives the point $(1,0)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}0&=(1+2)^2+k\\\\0&=9+k\\\\k&=-9\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$y=(x+2)^2-9.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 32
          },
          {
            "id": "p34-q15-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "e",
            "prompt": "has $y$-intercept $-6$,",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y=(x+2)^2-10$",
              "worked": "The $y$-intercept gives the point $(0,-6)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}-6&=(0+2)^2+k\\\\-6&=4+k\\\\k&=-10\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$y=(x+2)^2-10.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 32
          },
          {
            "id": "p34-q15-e",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "f",
            "prompt": "touches the line $y=-2$,",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y=(x+2)^2-2$",
              "worked": "The monic parabola opens upwards and has minimum value $k$ at its vertex. Touching the horizontal line $y=-2$ means $k=-2$.\n\n$$y=(x+2)^2-2.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 24
          },
          {
            "id": "p34-q15-f",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "g",
            "prompt": "has range $y\\ge7$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y=(x+2)^2+7$",
              "worked": "Since $(x+2)^2\\ge0$, the range of $y=(x+2)^2+k$ is $y\\ge k$. Thus $k=7$.\n\n$$y=(x+2)^2+7.$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 24
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
